# Locally: copy to .dev.vars for `npm run dev`. In production every value here is
# a SECRET (`npx wrangler secret put NAME`) — never a `var` in wrangler.jsonc,
# where a plaintext value silently wins over a secret of the same name.
#
# The "Deploy to Cloudflare" button asks for the uncommented names below.
# Everything else a deployment needs, `npm run deploy` sets on its own.

# ── RealtimeKit (Cloudflare Realtime) — needed for calls to start ─────────────
# 1. https://dash.cloudflare.com/?to=/:account/realtime/kit → Create App → copy the
#    App ID. Create it in the dashboard, not through the API: that is what creates
#    the default presets this code expects.
# 2. https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens → Create Token → the
#    "Realtime → RealtimeKit Admin" permission → copy the token.
# 3. Your account id is on the dashboard's overview page. `npm run deploy` fills
#    it in when it can work it out; the button flow may ask you for it.
REALTIMEKIT_APP_ID=
REALTIMEKIT_API_TOKEN=
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=

# ── Session signing ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Any long random string; rotating it signs everyone out. Generated by
# `npm run deploy` on a deployment that has none. On localhost the Worker uses
# a built-in dev value, so nothing is needed here for `npm run dev`.
# SESSION_SECRET=

# ── Local development ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The local seed (npm run db:seed) creates an admin you can sign in with:
#   email dev@example.com   password local-dev-password
# The Worker derives its own URL from each request, so nothing to set here.

# ── Cloudflare Access sign-in (only with HOST_AUTH_MODE=access) ────────────────
# See README "Authentication". Prefer it in production when you can.
# CF_ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN=yourteam.cloudflareaccess.com
# CF_ACCESS_AUD=
# ALLOWED_HOST_EMAIL=you@example.com,colleague@example.com
